  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following statements are correct?<br />\r<math><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> A <math>\r <mtext>&#x03C3;</mtext>\r</math>\r bond is stronger than a <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> bond<br />\r<math><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> A covalent bond is stronger than a hydrrogen bond<br />\r<math><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math> HF is more polar than HCl<br />\r<math><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo></math> There is one electrovalent bond and three covalent bonds in methylene chloride<br />\rSelect the correct answer using the codes given below",
