  "solution": {
    "text": "Here statement 1, 2 and 3 are correct while 4 is incorrect as in methylene chloride <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> , all four bonds are covalent. <br/>A <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">σ</mi></math> and covalent bond are stronger than a <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> bond due to stronger overlapping. <br/>HF is more polar than HCl due to more electronegativity difference.",
